  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 103.23 Fire protection",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 103.23 “Fire protection” means one or more fire hydrants installed on a water system’s water distribution system that are sized and configured with the intent that they will be capable of supplying a sufficient quantity of water with adequate pressure for fighting fires.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Dw 100) #10606, eff 6-1-14",
